# Scenario 2 - Split-Brain DNS

## Architecture

```text
                Internet Users
                       │
                       ▼
             app.contoso.com
                       │
                       ▼
                  52.1.1.10


═══════════════════════════════════════


                Internal Users
                       │
                       ▼
             app.contoso.com
                       │
                       ▼
                  10.1.1.10
```

## Requirements

- Internal users must stay on the private network.
- External users must access the public application.
- Both groups use the same FQDN.

## Question

Which DNS solution is being used?

A. DNS Forwarding

B. Auto Registration

C. Split-Brain DNS

D. Conditional Forwarding

<details>
<summary>Answer</summary>

✅ **C**

The same hostname exists in both public and private DNS zones, returning different IP addresses depending on the source of the query.

</details>

