# Scenario 3 - Private Endpoint Resolution

## Architecture

```text
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ Storage Account             │
│ mystorage                   │
└────────────┬────────────────┘
             │
             │ Private Endpoint
             ▼
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ 10.1.1.5                    │
└────────────┬────────────────┘
             │
             ▼
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ VNet-A                      │
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

## Observations

✅ VMs can ping `10.1.1.5`

✅ Network connectivity works

❌ Users cannot resolve:

```text
mystorage.blob.core.windows.net
```

## Question

Which component is most likely missing?

A. NSG

B. Route Table

C. Private DNS Zone

D. VPN Gateway

<details>
<summary>Answer</summary>

✅ **C**

Private Endpoints almost always require Private DNS integration for name resolution.

Connectivity exists, but DNS does not.

</details>

