# Scenario 6 - Multi-VNet Name Resolution (AZ-700 Style)

## Architecture

```text
                    Private DNS Zone
                 corp.contoso.internal
                            │
        ┌───────────────────┴───────────────────┐
        │                                       │
        ▼                                       ▼
┌─────────────────┐                 ┌─────────────────┐
│ VNet-Hub        │                 │ VNet-Shared     │
│ Zone Linked     │                 │ Zone Linked     │
└────────┬────────┘                 └────────┬────────┘
         │                                   │
         │ Peering                           │
         │                                   │
┌────────▼────────┐                 ┌────────▼────────┐
│ VNet-App1       │                 │ VNet-App2       │
│ Not Linked      │                 │ Not Linked      │
└─────────────────┘                 └─────────────────┘
```

## Requirement

Both App VNets must resolve:

```text
db01.corp.contoso.internal
```

with the fewest administrative changes.

## Question

What should you do?

A. Create additional peering

B. Create UDRs

C. Link the Private DNS Zone to App1 and App2

D. Deploy Azure Firewall

<details>
<summary>Answer</summary>

✅ **C**

DNS resolution is controlled by DNS Zone Links, not network peering.

</details>

